.nh
.TH "SOROLENS" "1" "Nov 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
sorolens-watchdog-register - Register a contract for monitoring via the watchdog contract


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsorolens watchdog register  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Register a contract for monitoring by invoking the watchdog contract's
register_contract entry point on-chain.

.PP
 is the 'C...' address of the contract to monitor.
--name is stored as a Soroban Symbol (letters, digits and underscores, at
most 9 characters) and --interval is the expected health-check cadence
(e.g. 300s, 5m, 1h).

.PP
Credentials, in decreasing precedence:
  1. --secret-key or --source-account flag
  2. SOROLENS_WATCHDOG_SECRET environment variable
  3. a named account configured in the soroban CLI (--soroban-account)

.PP
The watchdog contract id comes from --watchdog-contract-id, the
SOROLENS_WATCHDOG_CONTRACT_ID environment variable, or the repository's
WATCHDOG_CONTRACT_ID.

.PP
Use --dry-run to print the soroban CLI invocation without executing it.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print the soroban CLI invocation without executing it

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for register

.PP
\fB--interval\fP=0s
	Expected health-check interval (e.g. 300s, 5m, 1h; must be > 0)

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	Registration name stored on-chain as a Soroban Symbol (letters, digits, underscores; max 9 chars)

.PP
\fB--network\fP="testnet"
	Stellar network (testnet, mainnet, futurenet)

.PP
\fB--network-passphrase\fP="Test SDF Network ; September 2015"
	Network passphrase

.PP
\fB--rpc-url\fP="https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org:443"
	Soroban RPC endpoint

.PP
\fB--secret-key\fP=""
	Stellar secret seed (S...); falls back to $SOROLENS_WATCHDOG_SECRET

.PP
\fB--simulate\fP[=false]
	Simulate the invocation instead of submitting it (no transaction is applied)

.PP
\fB--soroban-account\fP=""
	Named source account already configured in the soroban CLI (soroban keys add)

.PP
\fB--soroban-bin\fP="soroban"
	Path to the soroban CLI binary

.PP
\fB--source-account\fP=""
	Stellar secret seed or account address used to sign (alias of --secret-key)

.PP
\fB--watchdog-contract-id\fP=""
	Watchdog contract id (C...); defaults to $SOROLENS_WATCHDOG_CONTRACT_ID, then $WATCHDOG_CONTRACT_ID


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API key for authenticating with the Sorolens API

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Sorolens API base URL

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--output\fP=""
	Output format (table, json, yaml or jsonl)

.PP
\fB--plugin-api-key\fP[=false]
	When dispatching to a plugin, pass the active profile's API key as SOROLENS_API_KEY (off by default)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Configuration profile name (default: $SOROLENS_PROFILE, then the default profile)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	jq-style path filter applied to structured output (e.g. '.items[].name')

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=10s
	Request timeout


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Preview the invocation without sending it
  sorolens watchdog register CACX... --name my_app --interval 300s \\
    --watchdog-contract-id CAC2... --dry-run

  # Register on testnet using a secret key
  sorolens watchdog register CACX... --name my_app --interval 300s \\
    --watchdog-contract-id CAC2... --source-account SABC...

  # Use a soroban CLI key alias instead of a raw secret
  sorolens watchdog register CACX... --name my_app --interval 300s \\
    --watchdog-contract-id CAC2... --soroban-account deployer
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsorolens-watchdog(1)\fP
